<article class="detail-page"><a class="detail-back" href="/insights/">← Back to insights</a><div class="section-label">Supply Chain</div><h1>Building a Supply Chain from Scratch: A Practical 5-Phase Blueprint for D2C Brands</h1><div class="detail-content modal-body"><p>This is based on a real engagement where we built a complete supply chain for a D2C brand from zero to 10,000+ orders per month in 20 weeks.</p><h4>Phase 1 (Weeks 1–3): Diagnosis & Mapping</h4><p>Before designing anything, map current state. Identify every pain point, every manual workaround, every recurring failure. Interview the people who actually do the work — not just managers. The insights are always in the operational staff.</p><h4>Phase 2 (Weeks 4–7): Procurement Foundation</h4><p>Vendor evaluation matrix. Contract templates. Payment terms policy. Approval matrix. This is the foundation everything else depends on — skip it and every downstream problem becomes a procurement problem in disguise.</p><h4>Phase 3 (Weeks 8–12): Warehouse & Inventory</h4><p>ABC classification of SKUs. Location coding. SOP for receiving, put-away, picking, packing, dispatch. Cycle count schedule. Most businesses skip this and then wonder why inventory accuracy is poor and orders are delayed.</p><h4>Phase 4 (Weeks 13–17): Distribution Network</h4><p>3PL selection and onboarding with SLA-backed contracts. Route planning. Returns management process. The goal: 95%+ OTIF from day one of go-live.</p><h4>Phase 5 (Weeks 18–20): Go-Live & Handover</h4><p>Team training on every SOP. KPI dashboard built and live. Daily review rhythm established. 30-day hypercare period before handover to client team.</p></div><a class="btn-primary" href="/#contact">Request a Discovery Call →</a></article>
</Layout>
